---

🛡️ WAR ROOM RISK BRIEF — 23 JUNE 2025 (REVISED)

🔍 New Confirmed Data

Iran launched 40 Kheybar Shekan missiles at Israel, marking an unprecedented conventional barrage and causing civilian casualties .

Iran’s Majlis voted to close (but not yet enact) the Strait of Hormuz, with the Supreme National Security Council retaining final authority .

UNSC convened, pressing for de-escalation, while Russia/China demand an immediate ceasefire .



---

⚙️ Model Inputs — Calibration for Accuracy

Component	Previous	Revised	Rationale &amp; Source

E (Destructive Capability)	0.58	0.60	Kheybar Shekan missile volley (40 missiles), drones + bunker-buster exchanges 
H (Uncertainty &amp; Disinformation)	0.95	0.90	Hormuz vote non-binding, clear next steps; some clarity from IAEA (no radiation leaks) 
Weights (Ew / Hw)	0.4 / 0.6	0.4 / 0.6	Emphasis remains on volatility over raw firepower



---

🧮 Recomputed Doomsday Index

Index = 100 × (0.4 × 0.60 + 0.6 × 0.90)  
      = 100 × (0.24 + 0.54)  
      = 78 / 100

🟠 Current Score: 78/100 — High Risk (just below the 80 “critical” threshold).


---

🚦 Risk Zoning

Level	Range	Status

Green	0–39	Low
Yellow	40–59	Moderate
Orange	60–79	High (⚠️ current)
Red	80–100	Critical (Pre-war)



---

📆 Near-Term Outlook (Next 72 hrs)

Window	Key Trigger	E	H	Index

Next 24 h	Hormuz closure final vote; naval posturing	0.62	0.92	80.8 ⚠️
48 h	Possible convoy interdiction; proxy strikes	0.60	0.90	78
72 h	Diplomatic demarches vs. fresh retaliation	0.58	0.85	73.4



---

🔐 Bottom Line &amp; Recommendations

Revised EHDI = 78/100: remains in High Risk, but clarity on Hormuz vote tempers extreme uncertainty.

Immediate focus:

1. Confirm final SNSC decision on Hormuz.


2. Validate missile strike damages via multi-sensor intel (satellite, IAEA).


3. Amplify unified diplomatic messaging (U.S./EU/Russia/China) to cap H.





